---
to: "docs/standing-ladder/audit-trail.md"
sparql:
  claims: |
    PREFIX stl: <http://seanchatmangpt.github.io/packs/standing-ladder#>
    PREFIX dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/>
    SELECT ?claim ?aboutFact ?curName ?curIndex ?description WHERE {
      ?claim a stl:StandingClaim ; stl:aboutFact ?aboutFact ; stl:hasStanding ?curState .
      ?curState stl:stateName ?curName ; stl:stateIndex ?curIndex .
      OPTIONAL { ?claim dcterms:description ?description . }
    } ORDER BY ?claim
  transitions: |
    PREFIX stl: <http://seanchatmangpt.github.io/packs/standing-ladder#>
    SELECT ?claim ?order ?fromName ?toName ?evidenceRef WHERE {
      ?t a stl:StandingTransition ; stl:aboutClaim ?claim ;
         stl:fromState ?fs ; stl:toState ?ts ;
         stl:transitionOrder ?order ; stl:evidenceRef ?evidenceRef .
      ?fs stl:stateName ?fromName .
      ?ts stl:stateName ?toName .
    } ORDER BY ?claim ?order
---
# Standing ladder audit trail (echo, not hand-maintained prose)

Every row below echoes literals already stored in this consumer's own facts against
`standing-ladder-pack`'s vocabulary — nothing here is synthesized, per
`pack-authoring-pack`'s "templates echo, they never synthesize" rule. Every claim listed
here is admitted only because `gates/010_no_skipped_states.rq` confirmed it carries a real,
unbroken, evidenced `stl:StandingTransition` chain from `UNKNOWN` to its current standing —
a claim with a skipped rung or an empty `stl:evidenceRef` anywhere in that chain cannot
reach this document at all.

